FINDING D (nit; one instance, and the CLI cannot do better)
The reds do not say they are mutation records.
----------------------------------------------------------
09.log and 10.log carry `bisellium red`'s six-line header (behaviour,
command, exit, at, sella, tree) and no field naming the mutation they were
produced under. `bisellium red <opus> --behaviour <n> [--sella] [--studio]
[--repo] [--cwd] [--now] -- <cmd…>` has no flag for one, and the logs are
"never by hand", so the label could not have gone there. It lives in
05ba562's commit message ("M4/M5") and in the ci.test.ts comments above each
behaviour. I established provenance myself by byte-reproduction (above), so
nothing is unproven here — but a reader of the log alone cannot tell a
mutation red from a test-first red, and that distinction is the difference
between two very different evidentiary claims. A `--note <text>` on
`bisellium red` would close it.

