VERDICT
-------
PASS. All three round-2 blocking findings are cleared, each verified by
execution rather than by the diff: the spec gate is byte-identical to its
prior CLI-written value and the advisory it silenced fires again; the
--allow-dirty split is enforced by two independent behaviours whose reds
byte-reproduce from the two mutations they claim; and the usage banner, the
per-command constant and the pinned scan count agree, with drift failing in
both directions and the pin proven load-bearing. Round-2 advisories A1 and A2
are closed with mutations that previously survived. The certificate
ce11b763… recomputes at f858df0. Nine mutations in total, every one caught,
worktree restored to f858df0 after each.

What convinces me, specifically: M4 and M5 each turn exactly one of the two
new behaviours red and nothing else; the M3 survivor from round 2 is now
caught; and `node --import tsx packages/cli/src/main.ts ci --repo .` ran the
real pipeline on the real repo, named its failing step, and wrote nothing.

Before `bisellium done`: amend briefs/W-031.md (FINDING A). Before merge:
reconcile studio/opera/W-031.md by hand (FINDING C). Neither is a code change
and neither warrants a fourth round.
